    ],
    "complete": false,
    "clarification_required": true,
    "rationale": "The qualified read returned three current records. None of them says whether an incremental import can be resumed from its old receipt. The two idempotency-receipt records (429ebfbe from a queue probe, 5c53ca49 from an HTTP acceptance probe) agree that a repeated request key returns the first successful response stored in its receipt. Both are reviewed semantic facts with external-class sources, and the records state they are synthetic fixtures rather than real admission evidence. They cover replaying a request, not resuming an import, so they are related context only. The pagination repeated-token record (c7b17274) also qualified, but it is about stopping on a repeated cursor and does not touch receipts, so I left it out of the answer set. The two records most likely to answer the question are Delta resumption (5e84b6ba) and Resumable checkpoint (5d3439a6), both under session recovery. The reader excluded both because of conditions it could not check: one needs an unknown prerequisite and one needs an unknown session. No prerequisite or session context was supplied, and unknown conditions exclude a lesson rather than count as met. So I can't say from memory whether resuming with the old receipt is allowed, or what has to be true first. That also doesn't mean the question necessarily depends on those conditions. The transactions branch (component:src/transactions, about replay identity) was not expanded because no component context was given, so coverage is incomplete. To settle this, the user needs to supply the actual import session and any prerequisite state, such as whether the earlier checkpoint or base is still valid, and which component is involved, so those excluded records can be qualified again. Any answer should also be checked against the current code before relying on it."
  },
